{"title": "Sectional Mock #147 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>WXYZ is a quadrilateral. The length of diagonal WY is 32 cm. The sum of perpendicular drawn from vertex X and Z on the diagonal WY is 12 cm. What is the area of the quadrilateral?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>WXYZ &#2319;&#2325; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; WY &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 32 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2358;&#2368;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; X &#2324;&#2352; Z &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; WY &#2346;&#2352; &#2326;&#2368;&#2306;&#2330;&#2375; &#2327;&#2319; &#2354;&#2350;&#2381;&#2348; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; 12 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["160 sq. cm", "180 sq. cm", "192 sq. cm", "172 sq. cm"], "options_hi": ["160 sq. cm", "180 sq. cm", "192 sq. cm", "172 sq. cm"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let the length of perpendicular drawn from vertex X to WY = A cm</p><p>Therefore, the length of perpendicular drawn from vertex Z to WY = (12  -  A) cm</p><p>Area of quadrilateral = Area of triangle WZY + area of triangle WXY</p><p>= (1/2) * A * 32 + (1/2) * (12  -  A) * 32</p><p>= 16A + 192  -  16A</p><p>= 192 sq. cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the length of perpendicular drawn from vertex X to WY = A cm</p><p>Therefore, the length of perpendicular drawn from vertex Z to WY = (12  -  A) cm</p><p>Area of quadrilateral = Area of triangle WZY + area of triangle WXY</p><p>= (1/2) * A * 32 + (1/2) * (12  -  A) * 32</p><p>= 16A + 192  -  16A</p><p>= 192 sq. cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the sum of the greatest and smallest four  -  digit numbers that begins with 4 and ends with 2.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>1 &#2360;&#2375; 15 &#2340;&#2325; &#2309;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2344;&#2347;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376; - </p>", "options_en": ["8844", "9044", "9124", "8994"], "options_hi": ["30030", "28760", "32480", "25410"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>All positive multiples of 8 less than 45 = 8, 16, 24, 32, 40</p><p>Product = 8 * 16 * 24 * 32 * 40 = 8<sup>6</sup> * 15</p><p>Required value = &#8731;(8<sup>6</sup> * 15) = 64&#8731;15</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>All positive multiples of 8 less than 45 = 8, 16, 24, 32, 40</p><p>Product = 8 * 16 * 24 * 32 * 40 = 8<sup>6</sup> * 15</p><p>Required value = &#8731;(8<sup>6</sup> * 15) = 64&#8731;15</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>From a circular sheet of area 1386 cm<sup>2</sup>, 2 cm wide five circular rings of variable radius were cut. What percentage of the sheet remained?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>1386 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;2 &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; 2 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2358;&#2368;&#2335; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368;&#2351; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2306;&#2330; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2331;&#2354;&#2381;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366;&#2335;&#2375; &#2327;&#2319;&#2404; &#2358;&#2368;&#2335; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2348;&#2330;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["21.2%", "23.8%", "25.7%", "27.4%"], "options_hi": ["21.2%", "23.8%", "25.7%", "27.4%"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>As we know, area of circle = &#960;r<sup>2</sup>, where 'r' is the radius of the circle</p><p>=&gt; Radius of sheet = &radic;[(1386  X  7)/22] = &radic;441 = 21 cm</p><p>&#8757; 5 rings of 2 cm width is cut,</p><p>=&gt; Radius of remaining sheet = 21  -  5(2) = 11 cm</p><p>Area of remaining sheet = (22/7)  X  11  X  11 = 380.3 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>&#8756; Percentage of remaining sheet = (380.3/1386)  X  100 = 27.4%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>As we know, area of circle = &#960;r<sup>2</sup>, where 'r' is the radius of the circle</p><p>=&gt; Radius of sheet = &radic;[(1386  X  7)/22] = &radic;441 = 21 cm</p><p>&#8757; 5 rings of 2 cm width is cut,</p><p>=&gt; Radius of remaining sheet = 21  -  5(2) = 11 cm</p><p>Area of remaining sheet = (22/7)  X  11  X  11 = 380.3 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>&#8756; Percentage of remaining sheet = (380.3/1386)  X  100 = 27.4%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>A boat can travel 60 km downstream in 4 hours. If the speed of the boat in still water is 13 km/h, then in what time will it cover 30 km upstream?</p>", "q_hi": "&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; 60 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; 4 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2352; &#2332;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; 13 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2361; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; 30 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2327;&#2368;?", "options_en": ["2(8/11) hours", "3(4/7) hours", "2(4/7) hours", "3(5/7) hours"], "options_hi": ["2(8/11) &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "3(4/7) &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "2(4/7) &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "3(5/7) &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Downstream speed = 60 &div; 4 = 15 km/h</p><p>Speed of boat in still water = 13 km/h</p><p>Speed of current = 15  -  13 = 2 km/h</p><p>Upstream speed = 13  -  2 = 11 km/h</p><p>Time to cover 30 km upstream = 30 &div; 11 = 2(8/11) hours</p><p>Option (a) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Downstream speed = 60 &div; 4 = 15 km/h</p><p>Speed of boat in still water = 13 km/h</p><p>Speed of current = 15  -  13 = 2 km/h</p><p>Upstream speed = 13  -  2 = 11 km/h</p><p>Time to cover 30 km upstream = 30 &div; 11 = 2(8/11) hours</p><p>Option (a) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>(x<sup>3</sup> + (k<sup>2</sup> + 2)x<sup>2</sup> + (k + 1)x  -  10) is completely divisible by (x + 2). What is the value of k if k &lt; 0?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>(x<sup>3</sup> + (k<sup>2</sup> + 2)x<sup>2</sup> + (k + 1)x - 10), (x + 2) &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2352;&#2361; &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; k &lt; 0 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; k &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; ?</p>", "options_en": ["-1/2", "-2/3", "-3/2", "-3/4"], "options_hi": ["-1/2", "-2/3", "-3/2", "-3/4"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Since f(x) = (x<sup>3</sup> + (k<sup>2</sup> + 2)x<sup>2</sup> + (k + 1)x  -  10) is divisible by (x + 2)</p><p>So, f(&#8722; 2) = 0</p><p>=&gt; (&#8722;2)<sup>3</sup> + (k<sup>2</sup> + 2)*(&#8722;2)<sup>2</sup> + (k + 1)*(&#8722;2)  -  10 = 0</p><p>=&gt; 2k<sup>2</sup>  -  k  -  6 = 0</p><p>=&gt; (2k + 3)(k  -  2) = 0</p><p>As, k &lt; 0 so, k = &#8722; 3/2</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Since f(x) = (x<sup>3</sup> + (k<sup>2</sup> + 2)x<sup>2</sup> + (k + 1)x  -  10) is divisible by (x + 2)</p><p>So, f(&#8722; 2) = 0</p><p>=&gt; (&#8722;2)<sup>3</sup> + (k<sup>2</sup> + 2)*(&#8722;2)<sup>2</sup> + (k + 1)*(&#8722;2)  -  10 = 0</p><p>=&gt; 2k<sup>2</sup>  -  k  -  6 = 0</p><p>=&gt; (2k + 3)(k  -  2) = 0</p><p>As, k &lt; 0 so, k = &#8722; 3/2</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>Read the data carefully and answer the following question.</p><p><img width=576 height=336 id=\"Chart 4\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13982/image096.png\"></p><p>What is the ratio of income of persons A, C, and E together to the income of persons B and D together?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2310;&#2306;&#2325;&#2396;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2344;&#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357;&#2325; &#2309;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2358;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2342;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"576\" height=\"336\" id=\"Chart 4\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13982/image096.png\"></p><p>&#2319;&#2325;&#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; A, C, &#2324;&#2352; E &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351; &#2324;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325;&#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; B &#2324;&#2352; D &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["13: 12", "12: 11", "11: 10", "10: 9"], "options_hi": ["13: 12", "12: 11", "11: 10", "10: 9"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Sum of percentages of income of A, C, and E together = 24 + 12 + 16 = 52%</p><p>Sum of percentages of income of B and D together = 18 + 30 = 48%</p><p>Required ratio = 52: 48 = 13: 12</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Sum of percentages of income of A, C, and E together = 24 + 12 + 16 = 52%</p><p>Sum of percentages of income of B and D together = 18 + 30 = 48%</p><p>Required ratio = 52: 48 = 13: 12</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>M can run 5 m in the same time N runs 5.5 m. In a 4.4 km race, N beats M by:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>M &#2313;&#2360;&#2368; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 5 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2360; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; N 5.5 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; 4.4 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, N, M &#2325;&#2379; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2361;&#2352;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["300 m", "400 m", "200 m", "500 m"], "options_hi": ["300 &#2350;&#2368;", "400 &#2350;&#2368;", "200 &#2350;&#2368;", "500 &#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>In 5.5 m race, N beats M by 5.5 - 5 = 0.5 m</p><p>In 4 km race, N beats M by (0.5 x 4400/5.5) = 400 m</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>In 5.5 m race, N beats M by 5.5 - 5 = 0.5 m</p><p>In 4 km race, N beats M by (0.5 x 4400/5.5) = 400 m</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>The radius of a circle is 25 cm. The base of a triangle is equal to the radius of this circle and the height of the triangle is 40% more than its base. Find the area of the triangle.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 25 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; 40% &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["437.5 sq. cm", "410.2 sq. cm", "522.5 sq. cm", "501.2 sq. cm"], "options_hi": ["437.5 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "410.2 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "522.5 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "501.2 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Base of triangle = 25 cm</p><p>Height of triangle = 25 x 140/100 = 35 cm</p><p>Area of the triangle = (1/2) x base x height</p><p>= (1/2) x 25 x 35</p><p>= 437.5 sq. cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Base of triangle = 25 cm</p><p>Height of triangle = 25 x 140/100 = 35 cm</p><p>Area of the triangle = (1/2) x base x height</p><p>= (1/2) x 25 x 35</p><p>= 437.5 sq. cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Let U be the universal set and n(U) = 11. If a set A is such that n(A) = 4, and n(A') = X, then find the value of X<sup>2</sup> + 1.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2354;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; U &#2360;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2369;&#2330;&#2381;&#2330;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; n(U) = 11 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2350;&#2369;&#2330;&#2381;&#2330;&#2351; A &#2320;&#2360;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2325;&#2367; n(A) = 4, &#2324;&#2352; n(A') = X &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; X<sup>2</sup> + 1 &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["37", "50", "65", "257"], "options_hi": ["37", "50", "65", "257"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>We know that,</p><p>A <img width=15 height=12 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27664/image001.png\"> A' = U</p><p>Therefore,</p><p>n(A') = n(U)  -  n(A) = 11  -  4 = 7</p><p>So, X = 7</p><p>Now,</p><p>X<sup>2</sup> + 1 = 49 + 1 = 50</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>We know that,</p><p>A <img width=15 height=12 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27664/image001.png\"> A' = U</p><p>Therefore,</p><p>n(A') = n(U)  -  n(A) = 11  -  4 = 7</p><p>So, X = 7</p><p>Now,</p><p>X<sup>2</sup> + 1 = 49 + 1 = 50</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>If (a + 5) is an odd number, then what are the two other even numbers nearest to it?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>45 &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2350; 8 &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2343;&#2344;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2350;&#2325; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2332;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2344;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2366; &#2328;&#2344;&#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["a + 4, a + 3", "a, a - 1", "a + 1, a + 2", "a + 2, a + 4"], "options_hi": ["64&#8731;15", "32&#8731;15", "64&#8731;5", "16&#8731;15"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>For perfect cube, number of zeroes should be 3, 6, 9 etc.</p><p>(a) 1000000, since it has 6 zeroes, so cube root = 10<sup>3</sup></p><p>(b) 2160000 - 4 zeroes</p><p>(c) 194000 = 194 * 1000 =&gt; 194 is not a perfect cube)</p><p>(d) 12500000  -  5 zeroes</p><p>Hence, option 'a' is correct.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>For perfect cube, number of zeroes should be 3, 6, 9 etc.</p><p>(a) 1000000, since it has 6 zeroes, so cube root = 10<sup>3</sup></p><p>(b) 2160000 - 4 zeroes</p><p>(c) 194000 = 194 * 1000 =&gt; 194 is not a perfect cube)</p><p>(d) 12500000  -  5 zeroes</p><p>Hence, option 'a' is correct.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>M and N are running on a circular track of length 800 m. Speed of M is 31 m/s and speed of N is 21 m/s. They start from the same point at the same time in the same direction. After how much time will they meet again for the first time?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>M &#2324;&#2352; N 800 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2376;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2352;&#2361;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; M &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; 31 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;/&#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; N &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; 21 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;/&#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2368; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2368; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2360;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2368; &#2342;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2330;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2357;&#2375; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2368; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2347;&#2367;&#2352; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2375;&#2306;&#2327;&#2375;?</p>", "options_en": ["60 sec", "80 sec", "70 sec", "90 sec"], "options_hi": ["60 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "80 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "70 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "90 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Relative speed = 31  -  21 = 10 m/s</p><p>Distance = 800 m</p><p>Required time = 800/10 = 80 sec</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Relative speed = 31  -  21 = 10 m/s</p><p>Distance = 800 m</p><p>Required time = 800/10 = 80 sec</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>Study the data carefully and answer the following question:</p><p>Below line graph shows the number of Jeans and shirts sold by five shopkeepers:</p><p><img width=576 height=336 id=\"Chart 3\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15829/image014.png\"></p><p>The number of shirts sold by Q and E together is approximately what percentage more or less than the number of jeans sold by W and R together?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2310;&#2305;&#2325;&#2396;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2344;&#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357;&#2325; &#2309;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2358;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2342;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375; :</p><p>&#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; &#2310;&#2352;&#2375;&#2326; &#2346;&#2366;&#2305;&#2330; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2368;&#2306; &#2327;&#2312; &#2332;&#2368;&#2344;&#2381;&#2360;&#2379;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2358;&#2352;&#2381;&#2335;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; :</p><p><img width=\"576\" height=\"336\" id=\"Chart 3\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15829/image014.png\"></p><p>&#2319;&#2325;&#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; Q &#2324;&#2352; E &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2358;&#2352;&#2381;&#2335;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;, &#2319;&#2325;&#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; W &#2324;&#2352; R &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2332;&#2368;&#2344;&#2381;&#2360;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2350; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["8%", "12%", "18%", "20%"], "options_hi": ["8%", "12%", "18%", "20%"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>The number of shirts sold by Q and E together = 100 + 180 = 280</p><p>The number of jeans sold by W and R together = 80 + 180 = 260</p><p>So, required % = (280  -  260)/260 * 100 = 7.69% &#8776; 8%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The number of shirts sold by Q and E together = 100 + 180 = 280</p><p>The number of jeans sold by W and R together = 80 + 180 = 260</p><p>So, required % = (280  -  260)/260 * 100 = 7.69% &#8776; 8%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>Which of the following is a prime number?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2309;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["54", "39", "68", "89"], "options_hi": ["54", "39", "68", "89"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><b>Prime number:</b> Number which is divisible by only 1 and itself.</p><p>54 = 1 * 2 * 3 * 3 * 3</p><p>39 = 1 * 3 * 13</p><p>68 = 1 * 2 * 2 * 17</p><p>89 = 1 * 89</p><p>Hence, 89 is a prime number.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><b>Prime number:</b> Number which is divisible by only 1 and itself.</p><p>54 = 1 * 2 * 3 * 3 * 3</p><p>39 = 1 * 3 * 13</p><p>68 = 1 * 2 * 2 * 17</p><p>89 = 1 * 89</p><p>Hence, 89 is a prime number.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>A student got 112 marks in English, 102 marks in Hindi, 98 marks in Biology, and 88 marks in Maths. If the maximum marks of each subject are 120, then find the overall percentage of marks get.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; &#2309;&#2306;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2332;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 112 &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;, &#2361;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 102 &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;, &#2332;&#2368;&#2357; &#2357;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 98 &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2324;&#2352; &#2327;&#2339;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 88 &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2375;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2357;&#2367;&#2359;&#2351; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325;&#2340;&#2350; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; 120 &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["81.24%", "83.33%", "85.15%", "87.66%"], "options_hi": ["81.24%", "83.33%", "85.15%", "87.66%"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Total marks = 112 + 102 + 98 + 88</p><p>= 400</p><p>Hence, the required percentage = 83.33%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total marks = 112 + 102 + 98 + 88</p><p>= 400</p><p>Hence, the required percentage = 83.33%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>A and B run a race of 3 km. First, A gives B a head start of 600 m and beats him by 120 seconds. While coming back, A gives B a lead of 5 minutes and gets beaten by 500 m. What is the difference between the times in minutes in which A and B can run the race for one side separately?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>A &#2324;&#2352; B 3 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375;, A, B &#2325;&#2379; 600 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2348;&#2338;&#2364;&#2340; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; 120 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2360;&#2375; &#2361;&#2352;&#2366; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2366;&#2346;&#2360; &#2310;&#2340;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351;, A, B &#2325;&#2379; 5 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2325;&#2368; &#2348;&#2338;&#2364;&#2340; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; 500 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2368;&#2331;&#2375; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2340;&#2352;&#2347; &#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2327;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; (&#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["6 minutes", "5 minutes", "7 minutes", "4 minutes"], "options_hi": ["6 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "5 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "7 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "4 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>When A covers 3000 m, then B covers 2400 meters</p><p>Let the speed of A and B be 'x' m/ minutes and 'y' m/minutes</p><p>2400/y  -  3000/x = 120/60</p><p>2400/y  -  3000/x = 2 .... (i)</p><p>When A covers 2500 m, then B covers 3000 meters</p><p>3000/y  -  2500/x = 5 .... (ii)</p><p>Multiply (ii) by 6/5</p><p>3600/y  -  3000/x = 6 ... (iii)</p><p>From (i) and (iii)</p><p>1200/y = 4</p><p>y = 300 m/minutes</p><p>Time taken by B to cover 3000 m = 3000/300 = 10 minutes</p><p>2400/300  -  3000/x = 2</p><p>8  -  3000/x = 2</p><p>x = 3000/6 = 500 m/minutes</p><p>Time taken by A to cover 3000 m = 3000/500 = 6 minutes</p><p>Hence, the required difference = 10  -  6 = 4 minutes</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>When A covers 3000 m, then B covers 2400 meters</p><p>Let the speed of A and B be 'x' m/ minutes and 'y' m/minutes</p><p>2400/y  -  3000/x = 120/60</p><p>2400/y  -  3000/x = 2 .... (i)</p><p>When A covers 2500 m, then B covers 3000 meters</p><p>3000/y  -  2500/x = 5 .... (ii)</p><p>Multiply (ii) by 6/5</p><p>3600/y  -  3000/x = 6 ... (iii)</p><p>From (i) and (iii)</p><p>1200/y = 4</p><p>y = 300 m/minutes</p><p>Time taken by B to cover 3000 m = 3000/300 = 10 minutes</p><p>2400/300  -  3000/x = 2</p><p>8  -  3000/x = 2</p><p>x = 3000/6 = 500 m/minutes</p><p>Time taken by A to cover 3000 m = 3000/500 = 6 minutes</p><p>Hence, the required difference = 10  -  6 = 4 minutes</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>What is the fractional form of 17.24444?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>17.24444 &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2368; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["17(11/43)", "17(11/45)", "17(8/45)", "17(8/43)"], "options_hi": ["17(11/43)", "17(11/45)", "17(8/45)", "17(8/43)"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let X = 17.24444 = 17.2444 ...(i)</p><p>Then, 100X = 1724.4444 ...(ii)</p><p>On subtracting (i) from (ii), we get -</p><p>99X = 1707.2</p><p>Then, <b>X = 17(11/45)</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let X = 17.24444 = 17.2444 ...(i)</p><p>Then, 100X = 1724.4444 ...(ii)</p><p>On subtracting (i) from (ii), we get -</p><p>99X = 1707.2</p><p>Then, <b>X = 17(11/45)</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>In a 1260 m race, Naman beats Pawan by 280 m or 40 seconds. Find the sum of the speed of Pawan and Naman.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>1260 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2350;&#2344; &#2346;&#2357;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379; 280 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2351;&#2366; 40 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2360;&#2375; &#2361;&#2352;&#2366; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2346;&#2357;&#2344; &#2324;&#2352; &#2344;&#2350;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["15 m/s", "18 m/s", "16 m/s", "14 m/s"], "options_hi": ["15 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;/&#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2337;", "18 &#2350;&#2368;/&#2360;&#2375;", "16 &#2350;&#2368;/&#2360;&#2375;", "14 &#2350;&#2368;/&#2360;&#2375;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let the speed of Naman and Pawan are X m/s and Y m/s respectively.</p><p>1260/X = (1260  -  280)/Y</p><p>1260/X = 980/Y</p><p>9/X = 7/Y -------(1)</p><p>1260/Y  -  1260/X = 40</p><p>63/Y  -  63/X = 2 ------(2)</p><p>From equation (1) and (2)-</p><p>63/Y  -  49/X = 2</p><p>14/Y = 2</p><p>Y = 7 m/s</p><p>X = 9 m/s</p><p>Hence, the speed of Pawan and Naman = 7 + 9 = 16 m/s</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the speed of Naman and Pawan are X m/s and Y m/s respectively.</p><p>1260/X = (1260  -  280)/Y</p><p>1260/X = 980/Y</p><p>9/X = 7/Y -------(1)</p><p>1260/Y  -  1260/X = 40</p><p>63/Y  -  63/X = 2 ------(2)</p><p>From equation (1) and (2)-</p><p>63/Y  -  49/X = 2</p><p>14/Y = 2</p><p>Y = 7 m/s</p><p>X = 9 m/s</p><p>Hence, the speed of Pawan and Naman = 7 + 9 = 16 m/s</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>The cost of milk per litre is increased by 45%. By what percentage must Chikki reduce his consumption of milk so as not to increase his expenditure? (correct up to two decimal places).</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 45% &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2361;&#2369;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2330;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2325;&#2368; &#2326;&#2346;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319; &#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2367; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2326;&#2352;&#2381;&#2330; &#2344; &#2348;&#2338;&#2364;&#2375;? (&#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2340;&#2325; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;)&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["40.25%", "28.28%", "31.03%", "35.25%"], "options_hi": ["40.25%", "28.28%", "31.03%", "35.25%"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let the original cost price be Rs. 100/litre</p><p>And the new cost price be Rs. 145/litre</p><p>Increase in expenditure = Rs. 45</p><p>Consumption of milk should decrease by 45/145 * 100 = 31.03%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the original cost price be Rs. 100/litre</p><p>And the new cost price be Rs. 145/litre</p><p>Increase in expenditure = Rs. 45</p><p>Consumption of milk should decrease by 45/145 * 100 = 31.03%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>If X = 0.732<span style=\"text-decoration:overline\">84", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; X = 0.732<span style=\"text-decoration:overline\">84", "options_en": ["1108", "1102", "1112", "1116"], "options_hi": ["1108", "1102", "1112", "1116"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>21/28 = 0.75, 32/36 = 0.88</p><p>(a) 16/21 = 0.76, 0.88 &gt; 0.76 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(b) 15/19 = 0.78, 0.88 &gt; 0.78 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(c) 14/18 = 0.77, 0.88 &gt; 0.77 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(d) 18/25 = 0.72, 0.88 &gt; 0.72 &lt; 0.75</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>21/28 = 0.75, 32/36 = 0.88</p><p>(a) 16/21 = 0.76, 0.88 &gt; 0.76 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(b) 15/19 = 0.78, 0.88 &gt; 0.78 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(c) 14/18 = 0.77, 0.88 &gt; 0.77 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(d) 18/25 = 0.72, 0.88 &gt; 0.72 &lt; 0.75</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>Study the following information carefully and answer the related question.</p><p>Following bar-graph represents the marks obtained by four students in economics, geography and history. </p><p><img width=563 height=314 id=\"Chart 9\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p17361/image009.png\"></p><p>For whom, average marks obtained in economics and history are equal to marks obtained in geography? </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2344;&#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357;&#2325; &#2309;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2306;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343;&#2367;&#2340; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2358;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2342;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2342;&#2306;&#2337;-&#2310;&#2352;&#2375;&#2326; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2357;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341;&#2358;&#2366;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;, &#2349;&#2370;&#2327;&#2379;&#2354; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2340;&#2367;&#2361;&#2366;&#2360; &#2357;&#2367;&#2359;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"563\" height=\"314\" id=\"Chart 9\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p17361/image009.png\"></p><p>&#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341;&#2358;&#2366;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2340;&#2367;&#2361;&#2366;&#2360; &#2357;&#2367;&#2359;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;, &#2349;&#2370;&#2327;&#2379;&#2354; &#2357;&#2367;&#2359;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["A and C", "B", "A, C and D", "B and D"], "options_hi": ["A &#2324;&#2352; C", "B", "A, C &#2324;&#2352; D", "B &#2324;&#2352; D"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>From the graph, we get </p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Student</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Economics</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Geography</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">History</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">A</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">76</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">50</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">44</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">B</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">84</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">72</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">60</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">C</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">36</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">48</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">56</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">D</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">40</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">60</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">80</td></tr></table><p>Average marks obtained by A in economics and history = (76 + 44)/2 = 60 (more than A's marks in geography)</p><p>Average marks obtained by B in economics and history = (84 + 60)/2 = 72 <b>(equal to B's marks in geography)</b></p><p>Average marks obtained by C in economics and history = (36 + 56)/2 = 46 (less than C's marks in geography)</p><p>Average marks obtained by D in economics and history = (40 + 80)/2 = 60 <b>(equal to D's marks in geography)</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>From the graph, we get </p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Student</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Economics</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Geography</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">History</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">A</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">76</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">50</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">44</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">B</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">84</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">72</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">60</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">C</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">36</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">48</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">56</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">D</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">40</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">60</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">80</td></tr></table><p>Average marks obtained by A in economics and history = (76 + 44)/2 = 60 (more than A's marks in geography)</p><p>Average marks obtained by B in economics and history = (84 + 60)/2 = 72 <b>(equal to B's marks in geography)</b></p><p>Average marks obtained by C in economics and history = (36 + 56)/2 = 46 (less than C's marks in geography)</p><p>Average marks obtained by D in economics and history = (40 + 80)/2 = 60 <b>(equal to D's marks in geography)</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>If 13 is added to both the numerator and the denominator of a fraction, then the fraction becomes 25/29. If 9 is subtracted from both the numerator and the denominator of a fraction, then the fraction becomes 7/9. Find the original fraction. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2358; &#2324;&#2352; &#2361;&#2352; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 13 &#2332;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; 25/29 &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2358; &#2324;&#2352; &#2361;&#2352; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 9 &#2328;&#2335;&#2366; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; 7/9 &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["39/45", "37/46", "37/45", "39/46"], "options_hi": ["39/45", "37/46", "37/45", "39/46"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let the required original fraction be 'a/b'.</p><p>(a + 13)/ (b + 13) = 25/29 </p><p>29a + 377 = 25b + 325 </p><p>a = (25b -52)/29 </p><p>(a  -  9)/ (b  -  9) = 7/9 </p><p>9a  -  81 = 7b  -  63 </p><p>9 (25b  -  52)/ 29  -  81 = 7b  -  63 </p><p>225b  -  468  -  2349 = 203b  -  1827 </p><p>22b = 990 </p><p>b = 45 </p><p>a = (1125  -  52)/29 = 37 </p><p>Hence, the required fraction = 37/45.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the required original fraction be 'a/b'.</p><p>(a + 13)/ (b + 13) = 25/29 </p><p>29a + 377 = 25b + 325 </p><p>a = (25b -52)/29 </p><p>(a  -  9)/ (b  -  9) = 7/9 </p><p>9a  -  81 = 7b  -  63 </p><p>9 (25b  -  52)/ 29  -  81 = 7b  -  63 </p><p>225b  -  468  -  2349 = 203b  -  1827 </p><p>22b = 990 </p><p>b = 45 </p><p>a = (1125  -  52)/29 = 37 </p><p>Hence, the required fraction = 37/45.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>Tarun gives Hari a head-start of 60 seconds in a 2400 m race and still beats him by 40 seconds. If the speed of Hari is 6 m/s, find the speed of Tarun.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2340;&#2352;&#2369;&#2339; 2400 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2352;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; 60 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2310;&#2327;&#2375; &#2352;&#2361;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2347;&#2367;&#2352; &#2349;&#2368; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; 40 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2360;&#2375; &#2361;&#2352;&#2366; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2361;&#2352;&#2367; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; 6 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;/&#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2340;&#2352;&#2369;&#2339; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["8.5 m/s", "7.5 m/s", "8 m/s", "7 m/s"], "options_hi": ["8.5 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;/&#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2337;", "7.5 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;/&#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2337;", "8 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;/&#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2337;", "7 &#2350;&#2368;/&#2360;&#2375;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Hari's time = 2400 / 6 = 400 s</p><p>Tarun's time = 400 - 60 - 40 = 300 s</p><p>Tarun's speed = 2400 / 300 = 8 m/s</p><p>Option (c) is the correct answer</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Hari's time = 2400 / 6 = 400 s</p><p>Tarun's time = 400 - 60 - 40 = 300 s</p><p>Tarun's speed = 2400 / 300 = 8 m/s</p><p>Option (c) is the correct answer</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>Read the following data carefully and answer the following questions. The following pie chart shows the percentage distribution of five different fruits sold by shop A. The total fruits sold by shop A = 1600 kgs.</p><p><img width=576 height=336 id=\"Chart 4\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24968/image006.png\"></p><p>Find the average of the total number of Bananas, Mangos, and peaches together sold by shop A.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2337;&#2375;&#2335;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2344; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2338;&#2364;&#2375;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2358;&#2381;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2342;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2346;&#2366;&#2312; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2335; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344; A &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2375; &#2327;&#2319; &#2346;&#2366;&#2305;&#2330; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2347;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2357;&#2367;&#2340;&#2352;&#2339; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344; A &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2375; &#2327;&#2319; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2347;&#2354; = 1600 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;&#2404;</p><p><img width=576 height=336 id=\"Chart 4\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24968/image006.png\"></p><p>&#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344; A &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2375; &#2327;&#2319; &#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375;, &#2310;&#2350; &#2324;&#2352; &#2310;&#2337;&#2364;&#2370; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["366", "362", "364", "368"], "options_hi": ["366", "362", "364", "368"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>The percentage of Bananas sold by shop A = 18%</p><p>The percentage of Mangos sold by shop A = 26%</p><p>The percentage of Peaches sold by shop A = 25%</p><p>Hence, the required average = [1600 * (18 + 26 + 25) %/100]/ 3</p><p>= 16 * 69/3</p><p>= 368</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The percentage of Bananas sold by shop A = 18%</p><p>The percentage of Mangos sold by shop A = 26%</p><p>The percentage of Peaches sold by shop A = 25%</p><p>Hence, the required average = [1600 * (18 + 26 + 25) %/100]/ 3</p><p>= 16 * 69/3</p><p>= 368</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>A train 1920 meter long crosses a tunnel whose length is 1880 meters in 76 seconds. If a truck is running at a speed of 65 m/s towards the train and train is 575 meter away from the truck, then in how much time (in seconds) will the train meets the truck?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>1920 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; (m) &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344; 1880 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2369;&#2352;&#2306;&#2327; &#2325;&#2379; 76 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;, &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2323;&#2352; 65 m/s &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2360;&#2375; &#2351;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2352;&#2361;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344;, &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325; &#2360;&#2375; 575 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; (&#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;) &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325; &#2360;&#2375; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2375;&#2327;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["6", "5", "7", "4"], "options_hi": ["6", "5", "7", "4"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>The train can cover (1920 + 1880) = 3800 m distance in 76 seconds which means the speed of the train = 3800/76 = 50 m/s</p><p>Relative speed of truck and train = 50 + 65 = 115 m/s</p><p>To cover the distance of 575 meters, it will take = 575/115 = 5 seconds</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The train can cover (1920 + 1880) = 3800 m distance in 76 seconds which means the speed of the train = 3800/76 = 50 m/s</p><p>Relative speed of truck and train = 50 + 65 = 115 m/s</p><p>To cover the distance of 575 meters, it will take = 575/115 = 5 seconds</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>If the six-digit number 1319XY is divisible by 3, 7, and 11, then what is the value of (4y)<sup>x </sup>?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2331;&#2361; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 1319XY, 3, 7 &#2324;&#2352; 11 &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; (4y)<sup>x </sup> &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["1", "16", "4", "64"], "options_hi": ["1", "16", "4", "64"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>3 x 7 x 11 = 231 so the given number is also divisible by 231.</p><p>Now, let the number be 131999.</p><p>So, when we divide 131999 by 231, we get 98 as remainder.</p><p>Therefore, original number = 131999  -  98 = 131901</p><p>And hence X = 0 and Y = 1</p><p>Now,</p><p>(4y)<sup>x</sup> = 4<sup>0</sup> = 1</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>3 x 7 x 11 = 231 so the given number is also divisible by 231.</p><p>Now, let the number be 131999.</p><p>So, when we divide 131999 by 231, we get 98 as remainder.</p><p>Therefore, original number = 131999  -  98 = 131901</p><p>And hence X = 0 and Y = 1</p><p>Now,</p><p>(4y)<sup>x</sup> = 4<sup>0</sup> = 1</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}]}